# Generated harness screenshots / scratch artifacts
scratch/

# Feedback pins (F8 in-app hotkey) -- user-filed visual bug reports with
# screenshots; see feedback/ in the dev server.
feedback/

# Root-level screenshots (verification-run leftovers). Root only: pngs under
# public/, docs/screenshots/, src/assets/ etc. stay trackable.
/*.png

# User-customization assets: scans/recreations of REAL branded products
# (trademarked art) matched from online references. Never committed — the
# repo ships generic procedural fallbacks; see public/user-assets/README.md.
public/user-assets/*
!public/user-assets/README.md

# Remote Play: kiosk-donated media-server credentials for private instances
.remote-play-seed.json
.mcp.json

# ── Front door (this fork) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# server/.env holds SESSION_SECRET and TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY. Anyone with the
# first can mint a session as any user, including the owner; anyone with the
# second can decrypt every viewer's Plex token out of the database. Committing
# this file to a public fork hands both to the internet, permanently — git
# history keeps them even after a later deletion.
.env
.env.*
!server/.env.example

# The front door's database. Holds encrypted Plex tokens for everyone the owner
# shared a library with. Encrypted is not a reason to publish it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
store.db*

# Agent/editor scaffolding that is not part of the project.
.claude/
.impeccable/
.mcp.json
